        "original_id": "198b1eb7-9370-5d90-96ea-a5ddc6c51196",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Charlie Walker, George D. Hay\n- Organizations: Grand Ole Opry, Country Radio DJ Hall of Fame, WSM\n- Places: Copeville, Texas, Nashville, Tennessee\n- Topics: Country music, radio broadcasting\n\nFacts:\n- The Grand Ole Opry was founded on November 28, 1925, in Nashville, Tennessee, by George D. Hay as a one-hour radio \"barn dance\" on WSM.\n- Charlie Walker was born on November 2, 1926, in Copeville, Texas, and he was an American country musician.\n- Charlie Walker held membership in the Grand Ole Opry from 1967.\n- Charlie Walker was inducted into the Country Radio DJ Hall of Fame in 1981.\n- Charlie Walker died on September 12, 2008.",
